{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while fixing bug `c49a-225d-2bc0-4478` (`perplexed-jeanlike-kakarikis`).\n\n`check_wall_clock_asserts` did not flag `test_narrow_operation_persists_the_same_bytes_as_the_legacy_sequence`, which flaked on a wall-clock boundary. The flake mechanism is indirect: the test never asserts on a timestamp directly. Instead it asserts byte-equality between two files independently produced by `BindingStore.save()`, and each save stamps `created_at` / `updated_at` from the wall clock in product code (`BindingLifecycle.bind_confirm` -> `_now_iso`). When the two builds straddle a one-second boundary the serialized bytes differ.\n\nThis is a gate blind spot: a byte/text-equality assertion between separately produced artifacts can be a latent wall-clock flake even when no direct timestamp or elapsed-time assertion appears in the test.\n\n## Decision\n\nOperator-authorized default 2026-09-07: implement a syntactic, conservative proxy rule rather than whole-product timestamp provenance analysis. Rationale: `check_wall_clock_asserts` is an AST lint over tests, so it should flag the observable anti-pattern it can prove cheaply — unfrozen equality/inequality comparisons between two different `Path.read_bytes()` / `Path.read_text()` expressions — and leave product-code timestamp provenance to the developer's review of the finding. This keeps the change small, deterministic, and aligned with the checker architecture.\n\n## Scope\n\nExtend `scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py` to detect unescaped file-content equality comparisons in test ASTs:\n\n- fire on `assert left.read_bytes() == right.read_bytes()` / `!=`, and equivalent `read_text()` comparisons, when the two call receivers are not the same AST expression;\n- fire on intermediate variables assigned from different `read_bytes()` / `read_text()` receivers and then compared for equality/inequality;\n- do not fire when the enclosing test freezes the production clock seam with `monkeypatch.setattr(..., \"_now_iso\", ...)` or `monkeypatch.setattr(..., \"utc_now_iso\", ...)`;\n- do not fire when both sides read from the same receiver expression, because that is a deterministic self-comparison rather than independently produced artifacts.\n\nThe finding text should explain that the rule is a transitive wall-clock flake proxy and that tests comparing independently produced artifact bytes should freeze the clock or assert semantic fields instead.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Parsing product code to prove whether a compared artifact embeds timestamps.\n- Auditing all existing cross-artifact byte-equality tests beyond what the checker and its test suite exercise.\n- Adding a new configuration mechanism or suppression marker beyond the existing checker patterns.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` has a RED-first test proving the checker flags a direct equality/inequality comparison between two different `read_bytes()` or `read_text()` receivers in a test with no clock freeze.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` has a RED-first test proving the checker flags equality/inequality between variables assigned from different file-content read receivers.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` has contrast tests proving same-receiver comparisons and tests that freeze `_now_iso` / `utc_now_iso` are not flagged.\n- [ ] Existing upper-bound wall-clock assertion behavior and escapes remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Verification: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py` exits zero, followed before push by `make verify` with the worktree venv on `PATH`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788803950566934001,"uuid":"3dac8f73-ae67-4cfb-9255-2bbe769f9546"}